  "analysis": {
    "concerns": [
      "Brood outvalues Terran at Tier I and Tier II: Brood T1 avg_value=18.17 vs Terran 17.50 (diff -0.67), Brood T2 avg_value=26.25 vs Terran 25.75 (diff -0.50). Brood wins the foundational board more consistently in the early and mid game across both tiers.",
      "Brood Tier II lacks DOUBLE_STRIKE entirely (abilities: boost/commander/sweep only). Terran STRIKE FORCE has 2-deep comparison reach at Tier II, giving Terran an uncontested mid-board tool. This is a capability asymmetry not reflected in raw edge values.",
      "Terran Tier III has 4 distinct abilities (double_strike, phantom, pierce, surge) including the unique SURGE comeback mechanic. Brood Tier III has only 3 abilities (ambush_strike x2, rush, pierce) and no resilience/recovery tool, creating an asymmetric comeback gap when Brood falls behind in row scoring."
    ],
    "recommendations": [
      "Add 0.5-1 point to Terran T1 baseline to close the -0.67 avg_value gap: raise MINING COLONY west edge from 5 to 6 (edge_sum 14 -> 15), bringing Terran T1 avg_value from 17.50 to ~17.83.",
      "Give one Brood Tier II card DOUBLE_STRIKE (e.g. replace SWARM WING sweep with double_strike) to eliminate the uncontested mid-board reach advantage Terran holds at that tier.",
      "Add a SURGE-equivalent resilience ability to one Brood Tier III card (e.g. give SKIMMER a \"FRENZY: When losing more rows than opponent, +2 to all edges\") so both factions have a comeback mechanism at their highest-tempo tier."
    ]
  }
